  "method": "Isolated test instance (scripts/macos/test-instance.mjs) on the protocol fixture. Two project conversations created from the welcome screen (folders answered by the IPC trace), each first message typed and sent with a real Enter, each fixture approval card answered with a real mouse click. Every surface audited in the DOM with the cdp-language-audit.mjs markers, over visible text and over title, aria-label and placeholder; every attribute naming a modifier collected. Shortcuts dispatched as key events through the bridge (Input.dispatchKeyEvent, Cmd = modifiers 4, Ctrl = 2): they reach the page's keydown handlers, as a real key press in the focused window would; the OS-level handling of Cmd+Tab (the app switcher) is outside the page. Zoom measured as window.innerWidth in CSS pixels. Search typed with Input.insertText in the Cmd+K dialog. Replay on 3196ce2 (capability core:webview:allow-set-webview-zoom; the sidebar hint says Ctrl+Tab on every OS): the zoom keys are now expected to change the page zoom with no 'not allowed' console error, and the switch hint to name Ctrl+Tab, the shortcut the app obeys. modifierHintsSayCmd now accepts the two hints that name a real Control shortcut on macOS (Ctrl+C in the terminal, Ctrl+Tab between conversations). If the zoom keys left the width unchanged, the capability is checked by the equivalent IPC call (plugin:webview|set_webview_zoom).",
  "previousRun": {
    "file": "docs/evidence/2026-10-13-macos-closure/m0-11-language-navigation.json",
    "commit": "08b291d",
    "defectsThen": [
      "Sidebar hint said 'Cmd+Tab to switch conversations': Cmd+Tab left the conversation unchanged (and is the system app switcher), Ctrl+Tab switched (conversationSwitchMatchesItsHint false).",
